WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Micron's $44 billion quarter covers its fab spending without new outside cash. This is AI Chips &amp; Data Centres, episode 33. After the cash, the split in high band with memory, a live Ohio campus, and an Oregon emergency, then a $2 verdict, and on the horizon. Mark Murphy, Micron's chief financial officer, put capital spending in that fiscal fourth quarter at $10.8 billion, and free cash flow at $33.2 billion. Shattered.io reports the quarter

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:38.460
quarter ended August 28, 2025, produce $5.73 billion of operating cash flow, about 7.7 times

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:38.760
lower.

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:46.260
All of Fiscal 2025 brought $17.53 billion of operating cash flow, so this single quarter

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:48.560
is about two and a half times that full year.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:53.960
Murphy said customers handed over $12.3 billion of cash deposits in the quarter.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:01:00.580
Ajusted free cash flow in that year earlier quarter was $803 million, and the outlet flags

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:04.060
that the older figure is labeled adjusted while the new one is not.

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:09.700
Micron's investor relations notice set the report date at September 30, 2026.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:17.240
Jensen Huang told CNBC on October 22, he does not anticipate a memory surplus by 2029.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:25.240
Biggo Finance puts SK Heinex in the second quarter at 25% of DRAM, 50% of high-band with memory,

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:34.000
and 19% of NAND. Micron sat at 24% of DRAM, 18% of high-band with memory, and 15% of NAND.

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:43.240
Micron's fiscal fourth quarter revenue rose 379%, and gross margin moved from 44.7% to 86.8%.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:51.500
SK Heinex grew revenue 257% and lifted gross margin from 54% to 83% and both companies

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.320
draw about 73% of sales from DRAM.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:02:00.880
Nvidia and SK Heinex signed a July partnership valued at more than $500 billion, covering

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:03.640
memory supply and AI data center buildouts.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:09.680
Micron has 26 long-term agreements covering more than 35% of revenue through 2030.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:16.537
And,thropic is running production inference and reinforcement learning rollouts on Tranium-2 and Tranium-3.

00:02:17.017 --> 00:02:21.637
Semi-analysis says its engineers have been on Tranium-3 racks for a couple of weeks,

00:02:22.177 --> 00:02:27.397
hit bugs, and still call the direction right, while saying the stack is nowhere near CUDA's maturity.

00:02:27.857 --> 00:02:32.317
Tranium allocates up to 80,000 physical cores to automated quality control.

00:02:32.317 --> 00:02:39.297
Tech Power Up reports AMD's HIP RT 3.2 notes named Medusa Integrated Graphics under

00:02:39.297 --> 00:02:46.837
three architecture IDs, GFX 1170, GFX 1171, and GFX 115E.

00:02:47.357 --> 00:02:55.797
The 117X IDs are RDNA 4M, sitting in the GFX 11 family with RDNA 3 and 3.5, plus

00:02:55.797 --> 00:02:59.217
FP8 and BF8 conversion and new matrix instructions.

00:02:59.217 --> 00:03:07.157
Those IDs showed up in LLVM in February, GFX 1171 and 1172 targets landed in March.

00:03:07.837 --> 00:03:15.377
GFX 1171 merged into Mesa 26.3 in August, and RDNA 4M firmware followed later that

00:03:15.377 --> 00:03:25.017
month. GFX 115X is the RDNA 3.5 graphics in Strix Point and Strix Halo, so GFX 115E reads as

00:03:25.017 --> 00:03:27.817
at least one Medusa chip staying on that generation.

00:03:28.537 --> 00:03:33.337
HipRT feeds rendering apps such as Blender, and the notes are not a gaming performance claim.

00:03:34.444 --> 00:03:39.824
Meta's Prometheus campus in Ohio is energized in its first phase, which Data Center Dynamics

00:03:39.824 --> 00:03:43.964
reports has already live, and the campus has already been used to train Muse.

00:03:44.764 --> 00:03:50.104
Umatilla Oregon has declared a state of emergency over lost data center revenue amid a statewide

00:03:50.104 --> 00:03:50.544
ban.

00:03:50.984 --> 00:03:54.404
The city was counting on tax revenue due from Sabie and Amazon.

00:03:54.404 --> 00:04:00.865
on. ZTE has unveiled a data center module built for AI workloads, with rack power inside

00:04:00.865 --> 00:04:07.285
the module from 20 kilowatts to 60 kilowatts. SK Heinex has dropped IPO plans for solidigum

00:04:07.285 --> 00:04:13.345
and confirmed a solidigum 3D nan fab in the United States. Tom's hardware sites unfavorable

00:04:13.345 --> 00:04:18.865
stock market conditions and semiconductor share price trends. Biggo Finance says the review

00:04:18.865 --> 00:04:24.845
of a U.S. listing talked about at as much as $15 billion is suspended, that solidiggum's

00:04:24.845 --> 00:04:29.945
growth prospects and investment needs are unchanged, and that other funding options stay open.

00:04:30.545 --> 00:04:35.665
Josh Gilbert at E-Toro APAC said the move removes a governance worry and keeps solidiggum's

00:04:35.665 --> 00:04:42.418
value inside the company. Amy Bedani, arms chief marketing officer, told E.E. Times the jury's

00:04:42.418 --> 00:04:48.758
$2 nominal award validates arm in the Qualcomm fight. The jury gave $1 for a licensing breach

00:04:48.758 --> 00:04:54.998
and $1 for interference with Qualcomm's relationship with Metta and found for arm on the other allegations.

00:04:55.698 --> 00:05:02.918
Judge Mary Ellen Norraica called Qualcomm's bid to force good faith talks on arm's V10 architecture very, very drastic.

00:05:03.798 --> 00:05:08.718
Badani said a written ruling on the remaining antitrust and licensing claims could take several weeks.

00:05:09.198 --> 00:05:16.938
She said risk-5 is not getting meaningful traction outside China and tied growth there to state backing rather than commercial displacement.

00:05:16.938 --> 00:05:23.758
Qualcomm has acquired RISC-5 startup Akeana, and Mateo Valero of the Barcelona Supercomputing

00:05:23.758 --> 00:05:29.158
Center told EE Times that closed instruction sets such as ARM limit the freedom to add

00:05:29.158 --> 00:05:35.850
functions and cut power. TSMC will still pay each non-managerial employee a sports day bonus

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:43.470
of $30,000 new Taiwan dollars, about $923 US dollars, after Typhoon Champion cancelled Saturday's

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:49.390
event. Focused Taiwan reports Chairman and Chief Executive C-Way told staff in a Friday

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:55.610
email that the 2026 bonus is $5,000 new Taiwan dollars above last year's. Payment comes

00:05:55.610 --> 00:06:02.470
in November for people on the payroll as of May 31, 2026. Last year the bonus was $25,000

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:08.330
new Taiwan dollars. Overseas employees were included for the first time and the 2025 total

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:15.690
was about $1.875 billion new Taiwan dollars. Net profit for the first nine months was $2.42 trillion

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:24.550
new Taiwan dollars, up 68.5%. At an October 15th investor conference, TSMC forecast 2026 sales

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:33.041
up 44% in US dollar terms, against a July view of slightly higher than 40%. Atamara and IQE will

00:06:33.041 --> 00:06:38.521
co-optimize MST-enabled gallium nitride on silicon for radio-frequency volume markets.

00:06:39.121 --> 00:06:44.281
Semi-conductor digest says IQE will manufacture those wafers for foundry and integrated

00:06:44.281 --> 00:06:45.321
device customers.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:52.360
High numerical aperture extreme ultraviolet printing, as WCC FAFTEC recounts from Intel's

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:58.280
Chris Auth on the Dwarkech podcast, puts the space between features in a window from 16 nanometers

00:06:58.280 --> 00:06:59.120
down to 8.

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:03.900
And that window is what you take apart when you ask why one exposure can finish the layer.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:10.000
A pitch inside that span can be written in a single pass, one mask, one alignment, one dose.

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:16.180
If the design needs features closer than one exposure can hold, the foundry splits the pattern into stages.

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:21.120
Each stage hitting a looser pitch, and the two exposures together make the dense layout.

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:24.940
That second shot is double patterning extreme ultraviolet.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:29.340
It costs another pass, another mask, and an overlay budget between them.

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:31.800
Auth's lever is backside power.

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:36.840
The power wires leave the front of the wafer and land on the back, so the transistors

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:39.840
and the data wires no longer share the front with the power grid.

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:45.200
He says that relief lets Intel print the front directly with high numerical aperture tools,

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:49.920
and that a looser pitch also loosens the error budget because features do not have to land

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:50.380
as close.

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:56.740
He says TSMC, without backside power, still runs tighter pitches, cannot finish that layer

00:07:56.740 --> 00:08:00.780
in one high numerical aperture pass, and stays on double patterning.

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:06.580
Walk the gate, need a pitch between 16 and 8 nanometers, and his account says one exposure

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:07.180
prints it.

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:12.280
Need tighter than 8 nanometers, and the single exposure is outside the window, so the

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:14.940
flow drops back to two extreme ultraviolet passes.

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:21.220
Intel's bet is that moving power rearward keeps the front inside that 16-8 window, so the

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:22.540
second pass never starts.

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:28.580
Auth said 14A is an option in the process design kit today, discussed customer by customer,

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:30.880
which is narrower than a blanket release.

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:34.540
Earlier reports had put backside power on 18A.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:39.660
In his telling, the scanner pays only after backside power has already bought the pitch relief.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:45.620
Chief Technology Officer Pushkar Ranadeh, on the same podcast, Split Lethography From

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:45.960
Scale.

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:51.840
TSMC is a much larger wafer manufacturer today, and catching that scale will be slow

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:52.560
and gradual.

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:58.480
On technology, he said Intel is already there, maybe a few percent off on performance, power,

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:03.140
or area density, and that a few percent is a different problem from being a whole generation

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:03.720
behind.

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:06.140
His first condition is time and yield.

00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:10.560
build. You can miss by a few percent, but you have to be on time, and yields have to

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:16.840
be very high for very large, very rapid ramps. A clean single pass from 8 to 16 nanometers

00:09:16.840 --> 00:09:21.900
still loses if yield cannot fill that ramp, while the larger foundry is already shipping.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:28.380
Jack Cavalieros, also at Intel, described the stack of N-type and P-type transistors. The

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:34.600
approach IBM has tied to a 0.7 nanometer plan. Wires that used to run on the top or on

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:37.900
the bottom, now have to drop vertically between the transistors.

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:40.880
Those trenches get taller relative to their width.

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:44.880
Filling them gets harder, and empty trenches leave air gaps and holes.

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:50.800
Backside power can buy a single high numerical aperture pass and still fail once those vertical

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:54.240
interconnects, not the in-plane pitch, set the yield.

00:09:55.208 --> 00:10:02.068
On the horizon, November 2026 is when TSMC pays that $30,000 new Taiwan bonus to employees

00:10:02.068 --> 00:10:07.528
ities, who are on the payroll as of May 31st. Within several weeks, ARM expects the

00:10:07.528 --> 00:10:12.368
written ruling on the remaining antitrust and licensing claims. Before we go, watch

00:10:12.368 --> 00:10:17.748
whether UMATIL is emergency moves the statewide data center ban, or whether the Sabian Amazon

00:10:17.748 --> 00:10:23.108
tax revenue the city was counting on comes back. That's AI chips and data centers for today.

